From 8a27b212d4e15814ac504c7ef066a2478421a245 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abdulaziz <alanziabdulaziz4@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 01:55:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] gdn: in-place cache-writing GDN op for CPU recurrent
 decode (K == 1 gate)

New op form ggml_gated_delta_net_cache (op_params[2] = 1, src[6] = rows_in
I32[n_seqs], src[9] = rows_out I64[min(T,K)*n_seqs]): the CPU kernel reads
each sequence's state at cache row rows_in[seq], updates the live row
rows_out[seq] in place (no copy when the rows coincide) and writes snapshot
slots 1..min(T,K)-1 straight into the cache; the result carries the
attention scores only. No get_rows gather, no dst state planes, no
write-back cpy / set_rows per layer: 6 -> 2 state-sized moves per seq.

Graph side: llama_memory_recurrent_context::rs_inplace_ok(n_seqs), a
side-effect-free predicate (never calls s_copy, which consumes rs_idx):
!is_full && n == n_seqs && cells[head+i].src0 == head+i. Stored in
llm_graph_input_rs::rs_inplace and added to can_reuse_rs so a reused graph
can never be in the wrong mode. build_rs_cache_view(inplace) asserts the
extra relocation range is empty, which makes the documented rows-mode
ordering hazard unreachable for the in-place consumer.

Model side (qwen35): gdn_state_inplace_dev_ok (no GPU/IGPU device), the
gate gdn_state_rows_env && inplace_dev_ok && inp->rs_inplace && fused_ok
&& cparams.n_rs_seq == 0 (Stage 7A: K == 1 only), the Metal rows+SET_ROWS
mode kept for Metal-only machines; build_recurrent_attn gains the
state_inplace branch, every legacy branch is untouched and serves the
transition ubatches (join/leave/seq_cp/reorder) and the env switch.
GGML_GDN_STATE_GATHER=1 still forces the legacy gathered path (A/B).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
